@Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress = http://localhost:5290

### Seeded test users (also available at runtime via the request below) -----------------------------------
### RUR Editor (Both levels)     : 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001  Ana Petrova
### RUR Reviewer (Country only)  : 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000002  Marcus Ionescu
### RUR Reviewer (Regional only) : 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003  Elena Kova
### SOL Editor (Both levels)     : 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000004  Noah Bergman
### SOL Reviewer (Both levels)   : 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000005  Priya Shah
### No role grants at all        : 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000006  Diego Reyes

@editorRuritania = 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@reviewerRuritaniaCountry = 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@reviewerRuritaniaRegional = 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003

### 0. List seeded test users (no auth required - this endpoint only exists for this exercise)
GET {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/test-users
Accept: application/json

### 1. Create a Country Package roadmap for Ruritania (as the RUR Editor)
# @name createPackage
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

{
  "countryCode": "RUR",
  "title": "FY26 Country Package"
}

### 2. Read the package back (any authenticated seeded user)
@packageId = {{createPackage.response.body.id}}
GET {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

### 3. Upload the roadmap document for step 1 (Decision / Country)
# multipart boundary is handled by your REST client; if testing manually, use Swagger UI instead - it
# generates the multipart body for you. This request is illustrative of the shape.
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/1/document
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="roadmap-v1.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample-files/roadmap-v1.pdf
------boundary--

### 4. Submit step 1, naming the Country-level Reviewer. Idempotency-Key makes a retry of this exact
### request safe - replay it and you'll get back the same result instead of a 409.
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/1/submit
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}
Idempotency-Key: submit-step-1-{{packageId}}

{
  "approverOrRecipientUserId": "{{reviewerRuritaniaCountry}}"
}

### 5. Reviewer approves step 1 (as the named Country-level Reviewer)
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/1/decision
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{reviewerRuritaniaCountry}}
Idempotency-Key: decide-step-1-{{packageId}}

{
  "decision": "Approve",
  "comment": "Looks good - approved at country level."
}

### 5b. ...or, instead of approving, return it for revision (comment is required)
# POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/1/decision
# Content-Type: application/json
# X-User-Id: {{reviewerRuritaniaCountry}}
#
# {
#   "decision": "ReturnForRevision",
#   "comment": "Please add the missing annex before resubmitting."
# }

### 6. Submit step 2 (Information / Country) - completes immediately, no reviewer action needed
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/2/submit
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

{
  "approverOrRecipientUserId": "{{reviewerRuritaniaCountry}}"
}

### 7. Upload the document for step 3 (Decision / Regional)
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/3/document
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="roadmap-regional-v1.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample-files/roadmap-v1.pdf
------boundary--

### 8. Submit step 3, naming the Regional-level Reviewer
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/3/submit
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

{
  "approverOrRecipientUserId": "{{reviewerRuritaniaRegional}}"
}

### 9. Reviewer approves step 3
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/3/decision
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{reviewerRuritaniaRegional}}

{
  "decision": "Approve",
  "comment": "Approved at regional level."
}

### 10. Submit step 4 (Information / Regional) - package is now Completed
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/steps/4/submit
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

{
  "approverOrRecipientUserId": "{{reviewerRuritaniaRegional}}"
}

### 11. Read the completed package
GET {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

### 12. Read the full audit trail
GET {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}/audit-log
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

### --- RBAC failure examples -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 13. No X-User-Id header at all -> 401
GET {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages/{{packageId}}

### 14. A user with zero role grants cannot create a roadmap -> 403
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000006

{
  "countryCode": "RUR",
  "title": "Should be rejected"
}

### 15. The RUR Editor cannot create a roadmap for a country they don't hold Editor clearance for -> 403
POST {{Country_PackageAPI_HostAddress}}/api/v1/country-packages
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{editorRuritania}}

{
  "countryCode": "SOL",
  "title": "Should be rejected"
}
